  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Relay Process Monitor Capability",
      "text": "> **Stable `0.1.2` is verified on official DSH `0.1.5-rc.2`\n> and `0.1.6-alpha.1`.** No implementation adaptation was required; its peer\n> metadata declares both exact releases.\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/relay-dsh-plugin-monitor-process)\n[](https://github.com/yangbobo2021/relay-dsh-plugin-monitor-process/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n[](LICENSE)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Relay Process Monitor Capability",
      "text": "This extension supplies a read-only, identity-safe process status capability for\nAgent-authored Relay Monitor Bundles. It deliberately does not add a prebuilt Bundle\nType: the Agent discovers no process type, issues an authorized Process Handle, and\nuses the `relay-monitor-author` Skill to create a task-scoped Bundle.\n\nInstall the exact public release together with Monitor Core and Author:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Relay Process Monitor Capability",
      "text": "```bash\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.3-rc.1 plugin --profile web add --save-exact \\\n  relay-dsh-plugin-monitors@0.3.2-rc.1 \\\n  relay-dsh-plugin-monitor-process@0.1.3-rc.1 \\\n  relay-dsh-plugin-monitor-author@0.1.3-rc.1\n\nThe same artifacts retain compatibility with audited DSH `0.1.2-alpha.3` profiles.\n\nThe plugin issues opaque, Session- and project-bound Process Handles. A PID is\naccepted only at handle issuance and is never embedded in a custom Bundle."
    }
  ],
